/* ---------- drawing ----------
 Two coordinate sets per molecule: 'z' = skeletal (zig-zag) and 'x' = Lewis (straight, 90° branches).
 Branches never bend unless they have to: in Lewis they run straight in the direction they leave the parent,
 in skeletal they keep a regular zig-zag. The one deliberate bend is at a two-bonded O (ethers / esters).
 Every layout is checked for overlaps and near-overlaps; if no clean layout exists the molecule is regenerated. */
const D60=Math.PI/3,D90=Math.PI/2;
